00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:06.200
Monster Documentary

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:01.990
The humble Yeti, a creature
representative of this extreme region.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.700
Wait, where did this come from?

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.790
Let us observe them
in their native habitat.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:11.550
They spend their lives roaming
the tundra, hunting for food.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:15.590
In this desolate land, blanketed
in ice and snow year-round,

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:19.430
the yeti must remain nomadic
to feed themselves and their children.

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:24.480
Building a permanent home
is simply out of the question.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:30.560
And so, the yeti live in temporary
dwellings: igloos they build themselves.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.560
It's quite comfortable!
Why not try building one for yourself?

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.240
You'll be building yours in a similar
fashion. Use all the snow you like.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:39.700
I have to do it myself?!

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:42.030
Since there's no need
for security measures,

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:44.790
you should be able to manage it yourself.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:48.540
Building it yourself means no
construction costs and no material fees.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.840
You can build the home of your dreams
on some of the cheapest land available.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.380
All you need to put in
is a little hard work!

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.800
You know that makes this sound
really sketchy, right?

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:02.180
The lot stretches all the way to those
far mountains. Build wherever you like.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:02.970
And it's all mine?!

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.180
Land is quite cheap out here.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:08.190
Right, then, let's begin
work on your igloo.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.480
Around here's good.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.110
First, compress the snow with your feet.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:18.900
You'll want to find a patch of snow
with the right hardness and density.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:20.280
1: Compress the snow

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.200
This snow is suitable.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:25.700
Next, create blocks out of snow
and begin stacking them up.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:31.120
2: Create blocks and stack

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.960
Fill in any gaps with extra snow.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.870
The smaller you build it,
the warmer it will be inside.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:31.040
Got it.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:36.300
You'll build three rooms: the main room,
a storage space, and the entryway.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:39.630
Main Room

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:39.630
Storage

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:39.630
Entry

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:40.090
The main room should be a step
higher than the other rooms.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:43.800
Then, hang up seal pelts in the main room.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:48.390
They'll help keep out the cold!

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:48.470
3: Hang seal pelts

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.860
T'would seem the weather has cleared.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:57.190
Dearia! I'm finished!

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.320
Excellent work.

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:00.200
Aww, shucks.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.200
Now for the difficult part.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.070
Huh?

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:07.910
As I explained earlier,
this location is extremely isolated.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:11.210
However, that means that surviving
here can be quite difficult.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:14.630
I believe it'd be best for you
to experience that yourself.

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:17.050
Why don't you try to survive here
on your own for the next three days?

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:17.880
What?

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.760
Do try not to die!

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.840
Not another training arc!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.300
W-Wait, can I find a more
peaceful place to live?

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:26.600
This will build character.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.140
I don't <i>need </i>character!

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.520
I'll return in three days. Good luck!

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.270
W-Wait!

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:38.730
Guess I should go get some firewood.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:47.530
Honestly, I kinda think I can make it!

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:51.290
Oooh, reindeer!

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:52.960
I can eat them!

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:56.960
But how do I catch them?
Do I use a trap, or use my bare claws?

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:49.970
I-I'm stuck!

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:54.350
S-Someone, help me! Please, help!

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:58.770
I mean, I've never hunted before.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.980
I get all my meat from the butcher's shop.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:04.610
Guess I'll just head home for now.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.910
But how? The weather's so bad...

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:15.710
Where's my igloo? Where is it?!

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:19.750
It's a total whiteout.
I can't see anything!

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:22.210
There's something behind me!

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:30.720
Help! Let go of me!

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.230
Are you inviting me in?

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.060
Thank you so much!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:44.650
My, if it isn't Letty!

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:45.740
Huh?

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:49.910
I'm helping out with dinner.
Take off your coat and wait right there.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:55.620
Dearia! Thank goodness,
I thought I was a goner!

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:59.710
Wow, the inside of this igloo is so warm!

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:03.250
Actually, it's kind of hot...

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:04.380
All done.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:06.550
Huh? Dearia...

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:07.930
What are you doing?

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:11.850
What do you mean? I took my shirt off
because it was hot, that's all.

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:14.430
You can disrobe
if you're feeling hot, too.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.730
I mean, I can't take off
much more than I already did...

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:20.150
But the yeti's disrobed quite a bit.

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:21.190
Wait, he can do that?!

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:22.940
My, it's hot in here, isn't it?

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.440
And he talks!

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.240
Everyone else has disrobed.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.240
Cheers!

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.450
Wh-Why are the dwarves here?!

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:31.120
N-Not the heroes, too!

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:31.120
My, is it hot.

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.780
I-It's so hot in here!

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:37.120
Huh? The igloo's melting!

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:51.890
A dream?!

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:54.180
Thank goodness, it was all a dream...

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.850
Where am I?

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:02.520
I'm hungry...

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.320
I wish I had a fishing pole.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:07.820
How will I get food?

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:09.570
An egg?

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:11.360
I wonder what kind of egg it is.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:16.120
A yummy egg...

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:23.130
Wait, if I eat this, that makes me
an egg thief! Come on, Letty!

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:28.260
I'd be just as bad as any old
egg thief! I don't want that!

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:31.010
The only eggs fit for eating
are unfertilized eggs!

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:34.140
So don't worry, I'm <i>not </i>gonna eat you!

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:40.890
W-Well, okay, then I'm heading home.

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.440
Wait...

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:44.060
What?!

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:45.850
Set
Adrift

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:50.360
H-H-How do I get back?!
Do I swim?! I can't swim!

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:55.700
I don't even know if dragons
survive a plunge into icy water...

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.160
Don't give up!

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.160
You still have a future ahead of you!
I'm sure things will get better!

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:03.210
Don't leave me here alone!

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:05.540
One
day
later

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.840
Nothing got better.

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:12.090
I'm so hungry!

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:22.230
No, no, no, I'm not eating it!

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:26.400
Don't eat it, don't eat it,
don't eat it...

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.780
Don't eat...

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:38.370
...me!

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.420
A dragon?

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:57.300
Oh, you're awake.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.510
You all right?

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:01.560
Where am I?

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:02.430
Can you stand?

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:04.890
Y-Yeah, I'm okay.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:09.860
I'm Davy Jones. Who're you?

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:11.530
My name's Letty.

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:12.530
Good to meetcha.

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.820
Oh, likewise.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:22.910
I was lost in the cold, then ended up
floating in the ocean, but how...

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:25.330
That's right! I got eaten by a whale!

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.750
Right. You're inside that whale right now.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:33.670
What?! So are we just gonna get digested?!

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:36.880
Nooo! I don't wanna be digested!

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:38.390
Calm down.

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:40.260
I said, calm down!

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:43.100
For someone so big,
you sure are a scaredy-cat.

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:44.310
But I'm gonna die...

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:45.640
C'mere.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:49.480
Lemme show you something.

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:58.110
Come in.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:59.870
Wait, really?

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:02.120
You'll be fine. C'mon.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:06.500
Whoa!

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:08.370
This here's my room. Come on in.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:10.170
O-Okay, thanks.

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:14.050
Whoa, it's squishy!

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:15.460
Want some tea?

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:18.720
Wait, how'd you get tea inside a whale?!

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:23.430
It swallowed up some boxes
that fell off a sinking ship.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:24.680
We've got more than just tea.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:28.940
Gems, eating utensils, cooking
ingredients, even gunpowder!

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:31.230
Th-Thank you!

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.980
Boy, is it warm in here.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:38.610
Kinda stuffy, but warm.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:42.490
The sea outside might be freezin',
but it's nice and warm in here.

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:45.120
Winter's warm, and summer's cool.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:46.700
Wow...

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.460
And heroes never come a-callin'.

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:51.250
That's nice.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:53.340
Though it kinda stinks in here.

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:58.260
What were you doin' out
in the middle of the ocean, though?

00:12:58.260 --> 00:12:59.760
Well, about that...

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:05.720
Sounds rough, tryin' to find
your perfect home.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:08.430
Guess even dragons can be picky sometimes.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:09.980
Yeah, sorry.

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:12.810
Dunno if it'd help give you ideas,
but do you wanna take a tour?

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.060
You don't mind?!

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:16.110
Not at all. Come along.

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:20.820
Here's our laundry room.

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:24.410
What's this?

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:25.370
The washing machine.

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:27.040
Really?

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:31.750
You put clothes in and
it washes 'em on its own.

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:33.210
How does that work?

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.420
Wh-What's that noise?!

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:45.220
That's the whale cryin' out.
The vibrations clean off all the gunk.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:47.010
Wh-Whoa, cool.

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:49.180
So it's an ultrasonic cleaning machine.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:51.850
This here's where we dry our clothes.

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:53.020
Watch.

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:55.360
Huh? Watch what?

00:13:58.070 --> 00:13:59.860
It's a big ol' wind tunnel.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:03.910
Whenever the whale breathes,
the air dries our clothes in an instant.

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:05.240
Wow.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:07.530
And probably makes them stink, too.

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:10.000
Here's our fuel storage.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:16.420
We use the whale's fat to light lamps,
cook with, and make soap.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:18.550
Cool!

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:21.510
Plus, it helps the whale shed
a couple pounds, too!

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:23.880
I dunno if I'd call that a win-win...

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:26.510
Here's our kitchen.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.810
We got fresh fish the whale swallowed up.

00:14:29.810 --> 00:14:31.310
A whole boatful, even!

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:33.730
That's awesome!

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:35.560
I'll make us a feast for the ages tonight.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:39.020
Really? 'Cause I'm pretty hungry!

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:43.360
Thanks for cooking for me!

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:49.370
Hey, thanks. Bath's filled and
ready whenever you want.

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:51.790
Huh? You've even got a bath?

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:55.290
It's a little lukewarm.

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:58.630
Like, kind of gross, but also feels nice.

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:01.340
It's warmed up using
the whale's body heat.

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:02.970
Don't look a gift horse in the mouth.

00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:06.430
Oh, right. You wanna
stay here a while, Letty?

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:08.390
Huh? Oh, no, I couldn't!

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:11.390
You could, it's all good. I'm glad
to have someone around, anyway.

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:13.020
Stay as long as you like.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:18.520
Mr. Jones is such a nice guy.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:22.440
I've got a warm bed, too...
What a nice house.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:26.110
I wouldn't mind living
someplace like this.

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:33.370
I wonder if I'll ever
be able to get out, though.

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:35.000
Oh, Dearia...

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:48.970
Gotta pee... Where's the bathroom?

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:57.440
Mr. Jones? What is he
doing up at this hour?

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:04.230
Wh-Why is he sharpening his knife?!

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:06.280
Is he gonna eat me?!

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:12.450
Is he gonna cut me up
and feed me to the whale?!

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:18.120
Oh, no. Am I trapped here?
Is there no escape?

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.210
Letty?

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:23.960
Mornin'!

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:25.800
G-G-G-Good morning?

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:29.010
Breakfast's gonna be a bit.
I'm gettin' it ready now.

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:33.350
M-Mr. Jones, why are you
cooking this late at night?

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:34.850
It's morning.

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:37.940
We live in a whale. We don't see the sun.

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:39.060
Oh.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:39.900
Need the bathroom?

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:41.610
Oh, yes, please!

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:43.730
It's down that way on the left.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:44.730
On the left?

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:46.610
Once you're done, give the toilet a kick!

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.780
It'll flush on its own!

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:50.780
Wait, where does it flush to?

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:52.780
Out into the ocean!

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:54.790
But where does it come out from?

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:57.160
Don't ask! I'm tryin' to cook!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.830
Ah, you gotta get outta here, then?

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:06.170
Yeah. I need to take this egg
back to its parents.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:10.220
That, and someone's
waiting for me out there.

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:14.640
Well, that's too bad.
You could stay longer, y'know.

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:16.930
Thanks for the offer.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.730
So how're you planning on gettin' out?

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:22.520
Huh? You mean there
isn't a way out already?

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:27.440
No, there is, you can get out
if you want, just...

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:38.330
We're gonna blow you out the blowhole.

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:40.120
Hold up!

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:47.210
Huh? What's that, Mr. Jones?

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.510
It's not gunpowder, right?!

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:51.970
This? It's just pepper!

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:53.430
Wait, why pepper?

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:55.550
It makes 'im sneeze.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:57.430
That'll get you up and outta here.

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.270
And I'll survive that, right?!

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:03.400
Never had to blow out a dragon before.
Guess we'll have to give it a go.

00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:05.770
If you get stuck in there I might
not be able to get you down.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:07.690
Oh, jeez!

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:10.280
C'mon, man up! You're a dragon!

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:17.330
That little egg's countin' on you.

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:23.210
Right! Let's do this, then!

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:24.790
Here we go!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.130
Five,

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:27.800
four,

00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:29.550
three,

00:18:29.550 --> 00:18:31.260
two,

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:32.470
one.

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.590
Fire!

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:06.170
I-I'm alive!

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:07.750
The egg!

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:10.380
Oh, good, it's still in one piece!

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:15.430
I'm free! I'm finally free!

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:18.420
Set
Adrift
Again

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:21.060
I sure am hungry...

00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:34.450
Yes! I found me some food!

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:35.990
Okay, I'm gonna eat you!

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:40.620
I'm a big ol' dragon, after all!
I can kill a seal, easy!

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:44.910
C'mon now, instincts, take over and get it!
Don't let its cuteness fool you!

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.290
It's delicious meat! A big slab of meat!

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:54.340
I can't do it! It's too cute!

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:57.680
Perhaps you are indeed
ill-suited for this lifestyle.

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:00.260
Huh?!

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:01.680
Over here.

00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:10.360
Some in your situation would fall
right into the survivalist lifestyle...

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:13.730
...but you're a bit too much
of a city slicker, I think.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:17.360
I didn't know you were a seal, Dearia!
I thought you were an elf!

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:20.820
I <i>am </i>an elf. I just borrowed a pelt
from a selkie friend of mine.

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:23.490
Wearing it turns me into a seal.

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:25.250
Just for you, hon.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.580
Were you also the reindeer and rabbits?!

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.210
I didn't go that far, no.

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:34.510
I kept a close eye on you from afar
to ensure no harm came to you.

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:36.670
Oh, he just got swallowed by a whale.

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:36.670
Well, don't <i>you </i>look comfortable!

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:41.220
I thought the extreme conditions might
awaken your dragon sensibilities,

00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:45.180
but you're far too sweet
to survive in this environment.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.270
I'm sorry for testing you.

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:49.190
It's okay.

00:20:49.190 --> 00:20:51.650
This is the real you, though, right?
You're not gonna disrobe, right?!

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:53.110
Whatever are you talking about?

00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:56.900
What would you have done
if I'd actually tried to bite you?

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:58.240
Why, nothing at all.

00:20:58.240 --> 00:21:00.700
I would have been impressed...

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.030
...by how strong you'd become.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:04.740
Dearia!

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:08.250
Oh, Dearia!

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:15.500
That being said, it would take more
than that to sink your teeth into me.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.630
Figured...

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:22.300
Have some stew. It will help you warm up.

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:24.300
Thanks.

00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:27.470
Where did you find this egg?

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.440
I found it lying there in the snow,
and it ended up on the same ice floe as me.

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:33.270
Stop!

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:34.730
Are you allergic to eggs?

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:36.980
That's <i>not </i>why I'm freaking out!

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:42.070
I wanna take it back to its parents.

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:43.160
Wait, what?

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:52.920
Papa!

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:55.710
Papa! Papa! Papa!

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:56.840
Congratulations.

00:21:56.840 --> 00:21:57.840
It's not mine!

00:21:57.840 --> 00:21:59.920
Papa!

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:31.220
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:31.260
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:31.300
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:33.680
Have you ever built an igloo?

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:36.310
Here's a simple way to do it.

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:36.220
How to Build an Igloo

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:39.610
Stack a number of empty boxes,
then pack in snow around it.

00:23:39.610 --> 00:23:45.070
Wait for it to freeze, then remove the boxes,
and you've got yourself an igloo.

